  "published": "2026-11-17T01:01:34Z",
  "modified": "2026-11-17T01:01:34Z",
  "details": "- CVE-2026-6460: forbid ALTERing a column or composite type used by stored expressions, defaults, constraints or indexes; fix related locking races (partial mitigation)\n- CVE-2026-116307: PL/Perl: refuse to free a prepared query that is being executed\n- CVE-2026-116316: prevent creating types in pg_temp from restricted code\n- CVE-2026-116319: PL/Perl: don't save and re-use the temp context in return_next()\n- CVE-2026-116320: PL/Perl: hold a reference on a Perl array or hash while scanning it\n- CVE-2026-116326: PL/Perl: cope with errors thrown from tied or overloaded objects (stale sigjmp_buf)\n- CVE-2026-116330: pg_dump: make \\restrict keys protective in tar-format restore.sql and generate them from /dev/urandom\n- CVE-2026-116331: don't use MinMaxAggPath if the aggregate's input and output types don't match\n- CVE-2026-116332: fix use-after-free when a portal being set up is dropped, ignore not-yet-defined portals in pg_cursors\n- CVE-2026-116335: check that commutator/negator operators return the same data type, reset links to a dropped operator\n- CVE-2026-120139: protect against tuple size miscalculation via int32 overflow and harden allocations against wraparound\n- CVE-2026-120141: fix type confusion with materialized set-returning functions\n- CVE-2026-120147: dblink: refuse to use a connection that a dblink call is already using",
